        answer: "The Native American Housing Assistance and Self-Determination Act of 1996 created the Indian Housing Block Grant, a formula-driven grant that gives tribes control over federal housing dollars. Tribes allocate it through an Indian Housing Plan covering development, rehabilitation, homeownership, services, and infrastructure. It replaced the old rigid federal housing programs with a self-governance model, and it remains the backbone of tribal housing finance nationwide.",
